 "summary": "Strengthens the `private_broadcast` fuzz target by tracking transaction addition timestamps and peer confirmation times. It computes which transactions satisfy staleness timing conditions and asserts that `PrivateBroadcast::GetStale()` returns exactly the expected set rather than an arbitrary subset.",
 "problem": "The fuzz harness previously verified that transactions returned by `GetStale()` were valid candidates, but did not test completeness or timing rules. An implementation bug such as premature loop termination would omit stale transactions without failing tests, leading `ReattemptPrivateBroadcast()` to silently abandon transactions that need to be rebroadcast.",
 "evidence": [
  "Description notes that mutant 3752 on MutantHub (changing `continue` to `break` in `GetStale()`) passes all current tests without detection.",
  "Description notes that `ReattemptPrivateBroadcast()` only retries what `GetStale()` returns, so omitted stale transactions are never retried.",
  "PR discussion reference: partly came up during review in PR #35129."
